data premium = plan,usd; Basic,168; Plus,336; Premier,492; Family Max,756
chart bar premium unit=$ title="Annual employee premium" focus="Premier"

# Who each plan suits
- **Basic ($168 a year):** employees who want low cost and expect only checkups and cleanings.
- **Plus ($336 a year):** employees who expect some fillings or crowns and want a higher maximum, but need no orthodontia.
- **Premier ($492 a year):** families with children who may need braces, and anyone who wants a $2,500 maximum and a low deductible.
- **Family Max ($756 a year):** families with ongoing orthodontia who will use the higher $2,000 lifetime orthodontia maximum and $3,000 annual maximum.

# Recommendation
! Make Premier the default plan. It covers orthodontia for the 38 employees whose children need braces soon. Family Max costs $264 more a year and only pays off for families with ongoing orthodontia, so it stays available as an opt-in upgrade.
